message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "Kaizen-MRCA: a self-report cognitive risk model to prioritize referral to a memory unit"
version: 1.0.1
date-released: "2026-06-08"
repository-code: "https://github.com/fermarquez88/kaizen-mrca"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.20602277"
authors:
  - family-names: "Márquez"
    given-names: "Fernando"
    email: "fmarquez.mum@gmail.com"
    affiliation: "Neurology Service, Hospital Dr. Guillermo Rawson; Facultad de Ciencias Médicas, Universidad Católica de Cuyo, San Juan, Argentina"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - brain health
  - cognitive screening
  - social determinants of health
  - prediction models
  - health equity
  - TRIPOD+AI
abstract: >
  Self-report screening model that estimates the ACE-III total score and flags the risk of a low
  score, using the education-adjusted cut-off applied in practice, to prioritize referral to a public
  memory unit in San Juan, Argentina. Developed on the 2023 wave of the Neuromentia community
  screening program (n = 631) and validated temporally on the 2024 wave (n = 146). Not diagnostic;
  requires local recalibration.
